abstract: >-
  Pilot re-analysis of 50 face experiments and 17 text results separating
  generator release date from study date, a three-factor model (Turing Decay),
  and a preregistered meta-analysis of human detection of AI-generated audio
  and video (125 participant groups, 58 studies). People still detect AI audio
  and video about 17 percentage points above chance; audio sensitivity falls
  0.23 d' per year of newer generator; within text-to-video generators the
  margin above chance halves in about 1.3 years.
